& [PositiveRouting] returns canonical clauses only when the phase lock is valid and all local artifact hashes match
& [ExternalRouting] returns the fidelity record and selected Walking Attention byte locks while stating that the reviewed controller is an unsigned SJS candidate
& [ExperimentalRouting] returns ECS only as a candidate runtime projection with graph fallback and no selection authority
& [NegativeRouting] returns no live calendar, clock, provider, notification, background observer, Git mutation, concurrent agent, model training, database, desktop, FPGA, implementation, runtime, or external-effect authority
& [FreshnessRule] invalidates routing on CTPR source, SMTC authority, selected Walking Attention evidence, semantic, data, constraint, canonical, registry, or signature drift
